{"id":"house_me_2_paul-lepage","n":"Paul LePage","p":"Republican","race":{"mode":"house","st":"ME","d":"2","city":null},"updated":"2026-11-09","bio":"Paul Richard LePage (; born October 9, 1948) is an American businessman and politician who served as the 74th governor of Maine from 2011 to 2019. A member of the Republican Party, he also served as the mayor of Waterville, Maine, from 2004 to 2011.","bioSrc":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_LePage","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_LePage","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Paul_LePage_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/330px-Paul_LePage_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","imgSrc":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_LePage_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg","site":"http://www.maine.gov/governor/lepage/index.shtml","siteKind":"official","offices":["Governor of Maine (2011–2019)"],"qid":"Q881196"}